MCP-Telecom (Vendored, Modified)
==================================

This directory contains a modified version of MCP-Telecom, originally
created by Avinash Amudala.

  Upstream repository: https://github.com/Avinash-Amudala/MCP-Telecom
  Original license:    MIT (see LICENSE file in this directory)

Modifications made for the OTel 2.5 Telecom Tool-Calling Training project:

  1. Switched dependency from `mcp[cli]>=1.0.0` (MCP Python SDK v1.x) to
     standalone `fastmcp>=4.0.0` (PrefectHQ) for compatibility with the
     project's standard MCP framework.

  2. Changed transport from stdio to Streamable HTTP (MCP 2026-07-28 protocol).
     The server now listens on port 8000 via uvicorn ASGI. stdio support has
     been removed (HTTP-only).

  3. Added /healthz health endpoint returning JSON {"status": "ok"} for
     OpenShift liveness/readiness probes.

  4. Added device-inventory configuration scaffold (devices.yaml.example)
     with OpenShift Secret references for credential management.

  5. Added command-allowlist scaffold (command_allowlist.yaml) with
     deny-by-default safety mechanism for the safe CLI exec tool.

  6. Added httpx>=0.28.0 to dependencies for HTTP client support.

These modifications were made to support deploying MCP-Telecom on OpenShift
as part of the OTel 2.5 project's MCP Tooling Foundation (Phase 2).
